# Owners for the paths that can weaken ZZZ's own gates.
#
# `docs/src/development/review-policy.md` makes these paths high tier: a change
# here can silence the check that is supposed to catch it, so it needs an owner
# to sign off on top of the usual review. Everything else is owned by whoever
# reviews it, and adding a catch-all `*` entry would put one person in front of
# every pull request.
#
# Keep this list in sync with `TIERS["high"]` in `script/check-review-tier`.
# The classifier decides the tier; this file decides who must approve it.

# Workflows, templates, and the gate scripts they call.
/.github/                                    @BegoniaHe

# Repository gates. Editing one of these edits the review process itself.
/script/                                     @BegoniaHe

# Build tooling, including the `check` gate list.
/tooling/                                    @BegoniaHe

# Agent instructions: skills and agents change how future changes are written.
/.agents/                                    @BegoniaHe

# Project rules and the rejection ledger.
/.rules                                      @BegoniaHe
